--------------------------------------------------------------------
CURRENT ASSET STATUS  -  placeholders, not the client's work
--------------------------------------------------------------------
NO IMAGE CURRENTLY IN THIS REPOSITORY IS THE CLIENT'S WORK.

Every photograph is a stand-in fetched from Lorem Picsum, which serves
photography from Unsplash. They are here to test layout, legibility,
proportion and loading against real pictures, because procedural noise
cannot answer those questions.

They are used under the Unsplash License: free for commercial and
non-commercial use, no permission required, no attribution required.
That licence permits this use. It is not the reason they are leaving.

THEY MUST BE REMOVED BEFORE LAUNCH, and not because of any licence —
because a portfolio built from someone else's photographs misrepresents
the photographer whose name is on it. A visitor cannot tell a stand-in
from a portfolio piece, and one borrowed image quietly devalues every
real one beside it. This is why the site also carries no client name
while `live = false`.

CLIENT AND PROJECT NAMES ON THIS DEMO ARE INVENTED. No company named
anywhere on this site is, or has been, a client. A real company's name
on a demo implies a working relationship that does not exist, which is
the same reason no Microsoft asset appears here. If a name reads as a
real brand, it is a mistake and should be changed.

Every placeholder path is listed in tools/placeholders.py, so removing
them is one command with nothing left behind to wonder about:

    python3 tools/placeholders.py --purge

The generated icons and wallpapers under static/img/icons/ are a
separate matter: those are original work, drawn in tools/icons.py, and
may stay or be replaced as the client prefers.

